You are building Step 5 of the Clientloop Phase 1 UI shell plan. Full plan at `/Users/yashbaldha/.claude/plans/zany-mixing-flame.md`.

Project: `~/Clientloop`. Prior steps done: scaffold, mock data, shell, dashboard home (commit `ca1d8ed`).

## Context — read first
1. `~/Clientloop/lib/types.ts` — `Request`, `RequestStatus`, `Priority`, `getSlaStatus`, `Client`, `Assignee`
2. `~/Clientloop/lib/mock/requests.ts` — 20 requests across 4 statuses
3. `~/Clientloop/lib/mock/clients.ts` — 12 clients (denormalize by id for display)
4. `~/Clientloop/lib/mock/assignees.ts` — 4 team members
5. `~/Clientloop/app/(dashboard)/inbox/page.tsx` — placeholder, you will replace
6. `~/Clientloop/components/common/page-header.tsx` — reuse for title (has `actions` slot)
7. `~/Clientloop/components/common/empty-state.tsx` — reuse
8. `/Users/yashbaldha/.claude/memory/design/patterns/data-tables.md` — read the filter bar + table Card pattern
9. `/Users/yashbaldha/.claude/memory/patterns/good/ui-redesign-shadcn.md` — read table + badge sections

Key rules (non-negotiable):
- Filter bar in its OWN `<Card><CardContent p-4>`
- Table in SEPARATE `<Card className="overflow-hidden"><CardContent p-0>`
- Table rows `cursor-pointer hover:bg-muted/30`
- Action column: always-visible ghost icon buttons, NEVER hover-reveal
- Row click should NOT trigger when clicking action buttons (use `e.stopPropagation()`)
- Status badges: semantic variants (info/warning/success/muted) — if Badge CVA doesn't have them, add them
- Kanban is STATIC — no drag-and-drop library. Add `draggable` attribute + TODO comment on cards.
- Kanban responsive: `grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-4 gap-4`
- View toggle is CLIENT-SIDE state only, not a URL param (keeps Step 5 scope tight)
- NO `any`, NO `@ts-ignore`

## Scope — Step 5 ONLY

Build the inbox page with Table and Kanban views, toggle between them, client-side filters.

### 1. `components/inbox/status-badge.tsx` (server component)

```tsx
interface StatusBadgeProps { status: RequestStatus; }
```

Map:
- backlog → label "Backlog", blue tone: `bg-sky-100 text-sky-700 ring-1 ring-sky-200`
- in_progress → label "In Progress", gray: `bg-slate-100 text-slate-700 ring-1 ring-slate-200`
- review → label "Review", amber: `bg-amber-100 text-amber-800 ring-1 ring-amber-200`
- delivered → label "Delivered", emerald: `bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-700 ring-1 ring-emerald-200`

Use a typed `Record<RequestStatus, { label: string; className: string }>`.

Base classes: `inline-flex items-center rounded-full px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium whitespace-nowrap`

Also create `components/inbox/priority-badge.tsx` same pattern for `Priority`:
- low → muted gray
- normal → no badge actually, or a very subtle one; use `text-xs text-muted-foreground` plain text "Normal"
- high → amber
- urgent → red with small Flame icon

Keep both components small.

### 2. `components/inbox/view-toggle.tsx` (client component)

```tsx
"use client";
type ViewMode = "table" | "kanban";
interface ViewToggleProps { value: ViewMode; onChange: (v: ViewMode) => void; }
```

- Segmented control look: two buttons in a `<div className="inline-flex rounded-md border p-0.5 bg-muted/40">`
- Each button: `size-8 px-3 rounded-sm text-xs font-medium`, active has `bg-background shadow-sm`, inactive has `text-muted-foreground`
- Icons: Table2 for table, KanbanSquare for kanban (lucide)
- Label next to icon hidden on sm: `hidden sm:inline`

### 3. `components/inbox/filter-bar.tsx` (client component)

```tsx
"use client";
interface InboxFilters {
  search: string;
  status: RequestStatus | "all";
  priority: Priority | "all";
  clientId: string | "all";
}
interface FilterBarProps {
  filters: InboxFilters;
  onChange: (f: InboxFilters) => void;
  onClear: () => void;
  hasActiveFilters: boolean;
}
```

Layout in a `<Card><CardContent className="p-4">`:
- Row: flex wrap, gap-3, items-center
- Search input with `Search` icon (left absolute) — `w-full sm:w-64`
- Status shadcn `Select`: options = ["all", "backlog", "in_progress", "review", "delivered"]
- Priority shadcn `Select`: options = ["all", "urgent", "high", "normal", "low"]
- Client shadcn `Select`: options = "all" + list of clients (id → company name)
- "Clear filters" ghost button with X icon — only show when `hasActiveFilters === true`

Use proper Select items (SelectItem). Non-"all" values set the filter, "all" resets that field.

### 4. `components/inbox/inbox-table.tsx` (client component — or server if you can avoid state)

Actually can be server since filtering is done by parent. Make it a plain component taking pre-filtered requests. Rename: no need for `"use client"`.

```tsx
interface InboxTableProps {
  requests: readonly Request[];
  clients: readonly Client[];
  assignees: readonly Assignee[];
}
```

- Wrap table in `<Card className="overflow-hidden"><CardContent className="p-0">`
- Use shadcn `Table`, `TableHeader`, `TableRow`, `TableHead`, `TableBody`, `TableCell`
- Columns (desktop):
  1. Title — bold-ish (font-medium), max-w truncate
  2. Client — Avatar + company name
  3. Status — StatusBadge
  4. Priority — PriorityBadge
  5. Assignee — small Avatar with tooltip on hover (use shadcn Tooltip — optional, simpler: just initials in a rounded bg)
  6. SLA — chip showing "2h overdue" / "in 5h" / "3d" based on `getSlaStatus` + hours diff (use the anchor `2026-04-10T12:00:00Z`). Color: breached=red, warning=amber, ok=muted
  7. Created — relative "2d ago"
  8. Actions — 2 ghost icon buttons (Pencil, Archive) with `onClick={(e) => e.stopPropagation()}`; wrap the cell too with stopPropagation to be safe
- Row: `className="cursor-pointer hover:bg-muted/30"`
- Responsive: hide Priority and Assignee cols on md and below using `hidden md:table-cell`
- Footer row: "Showing X of Y" in muted-fg inside the card but below the table
- Empty state: if `requests.length === 0`, show the EmptyState component inside the card (icon Inbox, title "No matching requests", description "Try clearing your filters", action label "Clear filters")

### 5. `components/inbox/kanban-card.tsx` (server component)

```tsx
interface KanbanCardProps {
  request: Request;
  client: Client | undefined;
  assignee: Assignee | undefined;
}
```

- `<article draggable className="rounded-lg border bg-card p-3 shadow-sm hover:shadow transition cursor-grab active:cursor-grabbing">`
- Add `{/* TODO(phase2): wire drag-and-drop with dnd-kit */}`
- Top row: priority chip + SLA chip (right-aligned)
- Title: `text-sm font-medium line-clamp-2 mt-2`
- Raw message preview: `text-xs text-muted-foreground line-clamp-2 mt-1`
- Bottom row: client avatar+name (small) on left, assignee avatar on right

### 6. `components/inbox/inbox-kanban.tsx` (server component)

```tsx
interface InboxKanbanProps {
  requests: readonly Request[];
  clients: readonly Client[];
  assignees: readonly Assignee[];
}
```

- 4 columns: Backlog, In Progress, Review, Delivered — typed `const COLUMNS: readonly { id: RequestStatus; label: string }[]`
- `<div className="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-4 gap-4">`
- Each column: Card-ish div with header (label + count badge) + scrollable body (`max-h-[calc(100vh-20rem)] overflow-y-auto space-y-2 pr-1`)
- Header: `<div className="flex items-center justify-between px-1 pb-3"><h3 className="text-sm font-semibold">{col.label}</h3><span className="text-xs bg-muted rounded-full px-2 py-0.5">{count}</span></div>`
- Column bg: `rounded-xl bg-muted/30 p-3`
- Map requests filtered by column status to KanbanCard
- Empty column: small muted text "No requests"

### 7. `app/(dashboard)/inbox/page.tsx` — replace placeholder

Must be a `"use client"` page because it holds filter state and view toggle state. It's OK — we lose static rendering on /inbox but the shell stays SSR-capable.

```tsx
"use client";
import { useMemo, useState } from "react";
import { requests as allRequests, clients, assignees } from "@/lib/mock";
// imports...

export default function InboxPage() {
  const [view, setView] = useState<ViewMode>("table");
  const [filters, setFilters] = useState<InboxFilters>({ search: "", status: "all", priority: "all", clientId: "all" });

  const filtered = useMemo(() => {
    return allRequests.filter(r => {
      if (filters.status !== "all" && r.status !== filters.status) return false;
      if (filters.priority !== "all" && r.priority !== filters.priority) return false;
      if (filters.clientId !== "all" && r.clientId !== filters.clientId) return false;
      if (filters.search) {
        const q = filters.search.toLowerCase();
        if (!r.title.toLowerCase().includes(q) && !r.rawMessage.toLowerCase().includes(q)) return false;
      }
      return true;
    });
  }, [filters]);

  const hasActiveFilters = filters.search !== "" || filters.status !== "all" || filters.priority !== "all" || filters.clientId !== "all";

  return (
    <>
      <PageHeader
        title="Inbox"
        subtitle="All client requests in one place"
        actions={<ViewToggle value={view} onChange={setView} />}
      />
      <div className="space-y-4">
        <FilterBar filters={filters} onChange={setFilters} onClear={() => setFilters({ search: "", status: "all", priority: "all", clientId: "all" })} hasActiveFilters={hasActiveFilters} />
        {view === "table"
          ? <InboxTable requests={filtered} clients={clients} assignees={assignees} />
          : <InboxKanban requests={filtered} clients={clients} assignees={assignees} />}
      </div>
    </>
  );
}
```

### 8. Helper: `lib/utils/time.ts` (new file)

Create small typed helpers reusable across pages:
```ts
const ANCHOR = new Date("2026-04-10T12:00:00Z");
export function hoursFromNow(iso: string): number { /* signed hours, rounded to int */ }
export function formatSlaChip(slaDueAt: string): { label: string; tone: "ok" | "warning" | "breached" } { /* "2h overdue", "in 5h", "in 3d" */ }
export function formatRelative(iso: string): string { /* "2d ago", "3h ago" */ }
```

No `any`. Pure functions. Use this in Step 4's dashboard next time (don't touch dashboard now — just make it available).

Wait — dashboard Step 4 already has inline helpers. Don't refactor Step 4. Just use `lib/utils/time.ts` in Step 5 components. If Step 4's helpers duplicate — that's fine for now, Sage/Mira will flag in Step 9+11.

### 9. Verification

```
cd ~/Clientloop
pnpm tsc --noEmit
pnpm lint
pnpm build
pnpm dev &
sleep 3
curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" localhost:3000/inbox  # expect 200
kill %1
```

All must pass.

### 10. Commit

```
git add -A && git commit -m "feat(inbox): table + Kanban views, filter bar, status/priority badges"
```

## Hard rules recap
- NO `any`
- NO `@ts-ignore`
- NO `as X` assertions except `as const`
- NO hardcoded hex — use Tailwind palette utilities
- Action icons always visible, stopPropagation on click
- Kanban cards static draggable, no dnd lib
- Filter bar and table in SEPARATE cards
- Use existing `components/ui/*` primitives
- Respect `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` — guard array accesses

## Report back (under 300 words)
- Files created/modified
- tsc/lint/build results
- curl /inbox status
- Commit hash
- Any deviations and why

